<Layout frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <p>
    <strong
      >Sustainability Governance of China&#39;s Global Infrastructure
      Investments (SGAIN)</strong
    > is a £1.7 million research project awarded to <strong
      >Dr <a href="https://www.yixiansun.com">Yixian Sun</a></strong
    > at the University of Bath by the UKRI Future Leaders Fellowship.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our seven-year study programme integrates innovative mixed methods to assess
    China&#39;s efforts to promote green development through overseas
    infrastructure investments and also environmental and social impacts of key
    Chinese projects in different host contexts across the Global South. Our
    research aims to advance understanding of China&#39;s overseas engagement
    and its influence on global sustainable development. Our work will help
    policy practitioners develop suitable strategies to align international
    investments with local sustainability needs.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/research/">Learn more</a></p>
  <h1>
    <strong
      >Sustainability Governance of China&#39;s Global Infrastructure
      Investments</strong>
  </h1>
  <p>
    The project team includes leading researchers across the globe in the fields
    of international relations, environmental governance and development studies
    based at Fudan University (China), Universitas Gadjah Mada (Indonesia),
    University of Dhaka (Bangladesh), Sustainable Development Policy Institute
    (Pakistan), and National University of Singapore (Singapore).
  </p>
